<title>NETHERLANDS: POLYTHENE TO BUY WAVIN UNIT.</title>
<headline>POLYTHENE TO BUY WAVIN UNIT.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Polythene Plc said on Monday it planned to buy the industrial films and sacks business in Belgium and the Netherlands from Dutch Wavin BV, a 50 percent owned subsidiary of Royal Dutch/Shell .</p>
<p>The activities which Polythene plans to buy generated sales of 47 million stg last year, supplying markets in Germany, France and Britain.</p>
<p>Net assets and borrowings totalled 14 million stg at the end of last year and the company employed 340 people.</p>
<p>Wavin posted 1996 group turnover of 1.6 billion guilders in 1996.</p>
<p>A company spokesman said the intended sale was part of the ongoing process of concentrating on Wavin's core business of plastic pipes and pipe systems.</p>
<p>Last year the company sold its plastic crates and garbage bags subsidiaries.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
